  "note": "A bouncy shuffle: swing the eighths, long then short. Verse and chorus share one eight-bar pattern, E and D splitting a bar, a full bar of A, three times, then two bars of B. The quick E to D change is the thing to drill. B is a barre on the fifth string; B7 is an easier stand-in while you build it.",
